[
  {
    "id": "sitl04-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 36 Mode tables",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Set flight modes on ArduPilot and PX4 from each profile's mode table. ArduCopter GUIDED=4 vs PX4 encoded main/sub-mode bitfield — never cross-use mode numbers.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl04-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl04-tab",
    "name": "DO_SET_MODE per stack (ArduPilot small int vs PX4 bitfield)",
    "info": "ArduPilot sysid 1: set_mode GUIDED with params {\"1\":1,\"2\":4} (custom_mode 4).\nPX4 sysid 11: DO_SET_MODE POSCTL with params {\"1\":1,\"2\":3} — this SIH/image accepts the PX4 main_mode integer in param2. The packed HEARTBEAT bitfield (196608) is what the vehicle reports after the change, but sending 196608 as param2 is TEMPORARILY_REJECTED. Delivery=confirm (not complete) because completion compares param2 to peer flightMode and those encodings differ.\n\nLaunch ArduPilot:\n  sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter --out=udp:127.0.0.1:14550\nLaunch PX4 (ports version-specific; verify your build):\n  make px4_sitl gazebo\n  # set MAV_SYS_ID=11; point PX4 Connection at your GCS port (often 14550 broadcast or 14570/14580)\n\nArduPilot Connection: bind 0.0.0.0:14550 → remote 127.0.0.1:14551.\nPX4 Connection: bind 0.0.0.0:14560 → remote 127.0.0.1:14561.",
    "x": 300,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
